# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Tracked:   code, results (.json), splits.json, docs
# Not tracked: audio, model weights, feature dumps, participant data
#
# Two of the exclusions below are not about file size. Read the notes on
# PARTICIPANT DATA and CORPUS LICENSING before you relax them.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Audio and video ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.wav
*.webm
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.flac
*.ogg
*.mp4
*.avi
*.mov

audios/
audio/
videos/
PreprocessedAudio/
our_audios/
data/audios/
data/videos/
data/PreprocessedAudio/
data_public/audios/
data_public/PreprocessedAudio/
our_audios/

# ── Public corpora ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CORPUS LICENSING. Do not commit these even if a subset would fit.
# IEMOCAP is distributed under a signed USC agreement and may NOT be
# redistributed — that includes the label CSV, not only the audio. RAVDESS is
# CC BY-NC-SA and CREMA-D is ODbL; both require attribution and neither
# belongs in a code repository. Point to the download instructions instead.
ravdess/
cremad/
iemocap/
emodb/
RAVDESS_IEMOCAP_CREMAD/*/
iemocap_full_dataset.csv
*_full_release/

# ── Model weights ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# encoder.pt for wavlm-base-plus is ~380 MB, well over GitHub's 100 MB limit.
# The training log next to it IS tracked, so results stay reproducible.
# If a checkpoint has to be shared, use a release asset or Git LFS.
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.onnx
encoders/**/encoder.pt
checkpoints/

# ── Feature dumps and intermediates ────────────────────────────────────────
# features.jsonl holds a 768-d emotion2vec embedding per clip. Across the
# public corpora that is hundreds of megabytes, and 03 regenerates it.
features.jsonl
features_*.jsonl
*.features.jsonl
preprocess_manifest.jsonl

# Regenerated by 00 in seconds, and both embed ABSOLUTE paths from whichever
# machine ran it, so they are noise in a diff. utterances.jsonl also carries
# per-utterance IEMOCAP labels, which falls under the licensing note above.
utterances.jsonl
clip_sources.jsonl
embeddings/
*.npy
*.npz
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.parquet

# ── Participant data ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PRIVACY. These files carry Firebase UIDs for 16 real participants together
# with GAD-7 and PHQ-9 scores, which are clinical anxiety and depression
# screening instruments. That is identifiable human-subjects health data and
# it does not go in a repository, public or private, without an explicit
# ethics decision. Share it through whatever channel your ethics approval
# specifies, and keep aggregate results here instead.
metadata_records.json
predictions_per_video.json
predictions_emotion7
predictions_valence3
predictions_*.json
firebase_data/
*serviceAccount*.json
*firebase*credentials*.json
.env
.env.*
secrets.json

# ── Keep: results, splits, docs ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Negations come after the broad rules above, or they have no effect.
!results/
!results/**/*.json
!data/results/**/*.json
!data_public/results/**/*.json
!**/training_log.json

# splits.json defines the held-out speakers. It is small, and every number in
# the paper is meaningless if it is regenerated with a different seed. Track it.
!splits.json
!**/splits.json

!*.md
!requirements.txt

# ── Python ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version

# ── Notebooks ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*-checkpoint.ipynb

# ── Caches ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
huggingface/
transformers_cache/
torch_cache/
*.log
*.tmp
*.jsonl.tmp

# ── OS and editors ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~